          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em compactly supported distribution
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distribution"} distribution
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/support+of+a+distribution"} support of a distribution
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subset"} subset
          %p
            This implies that compactly supported distributions may be evaluated not just on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bump+functions"} bump functions
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+linear+functionals"} continuous linear functionals
            on the space of smooth functions (
            %a{:href => "#Hoermander90"}> Hörmander 90, theorem 2.3.1
            ).
          %p
            Therefore and since Schwartz’s notation for the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)
            of all smooth functions on the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}'(X)
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hoermander90"}> Hörmander 90, p. 45
            ).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#as_continuous_linear_duals_to_smooth_functions As continuous linear duals to smooth functions
          #TVSOfCompactlySupportedFunctions.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
                on a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{R}^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              for the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}
            %p
              Then the vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+vector+space"} Fréchet vector space
              induced by the family of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/seminorms"} seminorms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mn ∞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi p
                                  %mi K
                                  %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo ,
                            %mn ∞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Φ
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mi sup
                              %mrow
                                %mi x
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi K
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %msup
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi α
                              %mi Φ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
                    \&amp;\overset{p_{K}^\alpha}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    [0,\infty)
                    \\\
                    \\Phi &amp;\mapsto&amp; \underset{x \in K}{sup} {\vert \partial^\alpha \Phi(x) \vert}
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              indexed by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset \mathbb{R}^n
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+subset"} compact subset
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in \mathbb{N}^n
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuple"} tuple
              encoding the degrees of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivative"} partial derivative
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^\alpha
            %p
              Hence the seminorm
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi p
                      %mi K
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_K^\alpha
              sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supremum"} supremum
              over the points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in K
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+value"} absolute value
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+derivative"} partial derivative
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi α
                      %mi Φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial^\alpha \Phi
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
              defined thereby are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unions"} unions
              of translations of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighbourhood+base"} base
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+balls"} open balls
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo ,
                        %mi α
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ϵ
                      %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi p
                        %mi K
                        %mi α
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    B^\circ_{K,\alpha,\epsilon}(0)
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    v \in C^\infty\mathbb{R}^n
                    \\;\vert\;
                    p_K^\alpha(v)
                    \\lt
                    \\epsilon
                    \\right\}
            %p
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \in (0,\infty)
            %p We write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi TopVect
                      %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{E}(\mathbb{R}^n) \in TopVect_{\mathbb{R}}
            %p
              for the resulting
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+space"} Fréchet
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
          #CompactlySupportedDistributionsAsContinuousLinearDualsToBumpFunctions.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (compactly supported distributions as continuous linear duals to bump functions)
            %p
              The space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}'(\mathbb{R}^n)
              of
              %em compactly supported distributions
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+space"} dual space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{E}'(\mathbb{R}^n) \;\coloneqq\; \left(\mathcal{E}(\mathbb{R}^n)\right)^\ast
            %p
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              from def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TVSOfCompactlySupportedFunctions"}
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#Klainerman08"}> Klainerman 08, p. 9
            )
          %p This means the following
          #CharacterizationOfContinuityBySeminormBounds.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (characterization of continuity for compactly supported distributions)
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+function"} linear function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    u \;\colon\; C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n) \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}
            %p
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous
              with respect to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
              of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TVSOfCompactlySupportedFunctions"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CompactlySupportedDistributionsAsContinuousLinearDualsToBumpFunctions"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{E}(\mathbb{R}^n) \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}
            %p precisely if the following condition holds
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  there exists a compact subset
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset \mathbb{R}^n
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \in (0,\infty)
                  such that
                #eq:BoundBySumOfNormOfDerivatives.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo ∀
                          %mrow
                            %mi Φ
                            %mo ∈
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mn ∞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi u
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Φ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ≤
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi C
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi α
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mo ≤
                              %mi k
                          %munder
                            %mi sup
                            %mrow
                              %mi x
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %msup
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi α
                          %mi Φ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\underset{\Phi \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)}{\forall}
                        \\left(
                        \\vert u(\Phi) \vert
                        \\;\leq\;
                        C
                        \\underset{ {\vert \alpha \vert \leq k} }{\sum}
                        \\underset{x \in K}{sup} \vert \partial^\alpha \Phi \vert
                        \\right)
          %p
            (see also
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Hoermander90"} Hörmander 90, (2.3.2) and theorem 2.3.1
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By
              %a{:href => "locally+convex+topological+vector+space#AlternativeCharacterizationOfContinuityForLinearFunctionals"} this prop.
              the continuity of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is equivalent to there being an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi r
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ (K_1, \alpha_1), \cdots, (K_r, \alpha_r) \}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \in (0,\infty)
              such that
            #eq:BoundByMaximumOfSeminormsOverFiniteSet.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≤
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi C
                    %munder
                      %mi max
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mi sup
                        %mrow
                          %mi x
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi K
                            %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msup
                          %mo ∂
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi α
                              %mi i
                        %mi Φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert u(\Phi)\vert}
                    \\;\leq\;
                    C
                    \\underset{i = 1, \cdots, n}{max}
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{x \in K_i}{sup} {\vert \partial^{\alpha_i} \Phi \vert}
                    \\right)
            %p
              We need to see that this is equivalent to a bound of the form
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BoundBySumOfNormOfDerivatives"} (1)
            %p
              In one direction, assume that
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BoundByMaximumOfSeminormsOverFiniteSet"} (2)
              holds.
            %p
              The union
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo ∪
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \coloneqq \underset{i = 1, \cdots, n}{\cup} K_i
              is still a compact subset (
              %a{:href => "compact+space#UnionsAndIntersectionOfCompactSubspaces"}> this prop.
              ). Hence
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BoundByMaximumOfSeminormsOverFiniteSet"} (2)
              implies that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi u
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Φ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi C
                            %munder
                              %mi max
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo =
                                %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %mi ⋯
                                %mo ,
                                %mi n
                            %munder
                              %mi sup
                              %mrow
                                %mi x
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi K
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %msup
                                %mo ∂
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi α
                                    %mi i
                              %mi Φ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    {\vert u(\Phi)\vert}
                    \&amp; \leq
                    C
                    \\underset{i = 1, \cdots, n}{max}
                    \\underset{x \in K}{sup}
                    {\vert \partial^{\alpha_i} \Phi \vert}
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              and hence with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mi max
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \coloneqq \underset{i = 1, \cdots, n}{max} {\vert \alpha_i\vert}
              that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≤
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi C
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi α
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi k
                    %munder
                      %mi sup
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %msup
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi α
                      %mi Φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\vert u(\Phi)\vert}
                    \\;\leq\;
                    C
                    \\underset{{\vert \alpha\vert}  \leq k}{\sum}
                    \\underset{x \in K}{sup}
                    {\vert \partial^{\alpha} \Phi \vert}
                    \\,,
            %p
              which is of form
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BoundBySumOfNormOfDerivatives"} (1)
            %p
              Conversely, assume that a bound of the form
